win10xbox: heap_thread_detach() with the host process heap

The process heap is the host's (patch 0001) and every Rtl*Heap call is forwarded
to the host ntdll, so this ntdll never created a heap of its own and its static
process_heap is NULL. LdrShutdownThread() calls heap_thread_detach() on every
thread exit, which dereferenced that NULL (RtlEnterCriticalSection(NULL + 0xd0))
and killed the whole process the first time a guest thread returned. With no heap
of our own there are no low-fragmentation-heap bin groups to hand back.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/heap.c b/dlls/ntdll/heap.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/heap.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/heap.c
@@ -2021,5 +2021,7 @@ static void heap_thread_detach_bin_groups( struct heap *heap )
 void heap_thread_detach(void)
 {
     struct heap *heap;
 
+    if (!process_heap) return;
+
     RtlEnterCriticalSection( &process_heap->cs );
